## 4. 220-Point Confluence Scoring — Sacred

### 4.1 The system is deterministic and sacred

The 220-point scorer is **not modified by overlay systems**. The BTC Systemic Cascade Overlay (and any future overlay) may adjust **position sizing**, never the raw score. Any proposed change to point weights requires explicit human approval and a document update before code.

### 4.2 Scoring rules

- Funding Z-score is **non-linear** — predictive power exists only at statistical extremes (|Z| > 2.5 SD = full points; 1.5–2.5 SD = partial; < 1.5 SD = zero)
- Funding *costs* adjust the **leverage tier**, never the confluence score
- Directional conflict across agents triggers a conviction downgrade multiplier
- Scoring is integer arithmetic only; every point attribution is logged for audit
- Market Context is a **regime gate**, not an intraday predictor

### 4.3 Signal thresholds

⚠️ **CONFIRM** — thresholds and category splits from v2.1. Carry forward unless current scorer differs.

| Label | Score | Position size |
|---|---|---|
| STRONG | 180–220 | 5.0% |
| MODERATE | 150–179 | 3.5% |
| WEAK | 120–149 | 2.0% |
| NO TRADE | 0–119 | 0% |

