## 13. Code Style

- Verbose, explicit; variable names long and descriptive; no clever one-liners
- Maximum 40 lines per function — extract named helpers if approaching the limit
- Type hints on every parameter and return value — no exceptions
- Docstring on every function (Args / Returns / Raises)
- Files and variables `snake_case`, classes `PascalCase`, constants `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE`
- Prefix vocabulary: `fetch_` for external API calls, `calculate_` for pure logic, `send_` for outbound actions

### Error handling

Fail loud but gracefully. Every error logged with full detail via Loguru structured kwargs (no f-strings in loggers). The failing module returns a safe empty value. The system continues with reduced data and marks the provider as DEGRADED in Redis. Never swallow errors silently, never let one provider failure cascade into a system crash.

